The **branching ratio** for a neutral meson \(P^0\) of mass \(M\) decaying to \(\ell^+\ell^-\) can be written (to a very good approximation) as  

\[
\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
\mathcal{B}(P^0\!\to\!\ell^+\ell^-) &=
\frac{G_F^2\alpha^2}{16\pi^3}\,M\,\tau_{P}\,f_{P}^2
\sqrt{1-\frac{4m_\ell^2}{M^2}}\\
&\times \Bigl|
C_{10}^{\rm eff}\, \frac{2m_\ell}{M}+C_{P}^{\rm eff}\frac{M}{m_b+m_q}
+ C_{S}^{\rm eff}\frac{M}{m_b+m_q}\Bigr|^{\!2},
\end{aligned}
}
\]

The **branching ratio** (ignoring tiny CP‑violating effects) is

\[
\boxed{
\mathcal B(B_{q}^{0}\!\to\mu^{+}\mu^{-}) =
\frac{G_F^{\,2}\,\alpha^{2}}{16\pi^{3}}\,f_{B_q}^{2}\,M_{B_q}\,\tau_{B_q}\,
|V_{tb}V_{tq}^{*}|^{2}\,
\sqrt{1-\frac{4m_{\mu}^{2}}{M_{B_q}^{2}}}\;\n\Bigl| C_{10}^{\rm eff} + \frac{M_{B_q}^{2}}{2m_{\mu}(m_{b}+m_{q})}
\bigl(C_{P} - C_{P}^{\prime}\bigr) \Bigr|^{2}
}
\]

